WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.594 --> 00:00:19.578
rest of Barry's training went smoothly—until late in the day when he suddenly spun around and bumped into

2
00:00:19.698 --> 00:00:21.080
Ally. "Whoa!"

3
00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:25.583
she cried as she stumbled forward, a platter of meteor fries slipping from her grasp.

4
00:00:26.124 --> 00:00:30.728
Without thinking, Ally activated her levitation powers, sending the plate floating in midair.

5
00:00:31.168 --> 00:00:33.450
The customers inside the diner broke into applause.

6
00:00:34.871 --> 00:00:39.415
"We got to see one of those famous tricks that Gourmet Greta wrote about!"

7
00:00:39.855 --> 00:00:40.656
one customer said.

8
00:00:40.676 --> 00:00:42.638
"We're so lucky!"

9
00:00:43.038 --> 00:00:43.559
said another.

10
00:00:43.579 --> 00:00:46.621
"I heard she doesn't do the tricks very often."

11
00:00:48.983 --> 00:00:52.426
Ally bowed as if she'd done it all on purpose and then delivered the fries.

12
00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.032
Barry hurried after her as she headed for the counter.

13
00:01:01.376 --> 00:01:02.577
"That was amazing!

14
00:01:02.897 --> 00:01:04.738
When are you going to teach me how to do that trick?"

15
00:01:05.158 --> 00:01:06.158
he asked eagerly.

16
00:01:06.178 --> 00:01:08.679
"Never!" Ally thought.

17
00:01:09.099 --> 00:01:11.180
But she forced herself to smile patiently at him.

18
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:14.342
"After you've been here for a while," she said.

19
00:01:14.362 --> 00:01:18.203
"There's still a lot you have to learn about the menu and other stuff."

20
00:01:19.204 --> 00:01:21.105
"I'm a fast learner," Barry said.

21
00:01:21.125 --> 00:01:22.705
"Teach me now!"

22
00:01:23.286 --> 00:01:27.007
Luckily, before she had to reply, a customer at table five waved at Barry.

23
00:01:27.768 --> 00:01:28.208
"Excuse me!

24
00:01:28.228 --> 00:01:32.377
Waiter?" "Looks like table five needs you, Barry," Ally said.

25
00:01:34.018 --> 00:01:37.159
While Barry hurried over to his table, Ally ducked into the kitchen.

26
00:01:37.179 --> 00:01:41.021
"Yikes," she thought, blowing out a breath.

27
00:01:41.041 --> 00:01:43.322
"Barry is so persistent!"

28
00:01:45.623 --> 00:01:48.444
At the end of the day, Ray made a meal for all the workers.

29
00:01:49.104 --> 00:01:52.905
Ally, Randy, Ray, and Barry sat down in a booth to eat together.

30
00:01:52.925 --> 00:01:58.808
"This is delicious," Barry said, biting into his club sandwich.

31
00:01:59.468 --> 00:02:00.369
"What's your secret, Ray?"

32
00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:05.672
"Ray uses only the freshest ingredients," Randy said.

33
00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:07.714
"Not that."

34
00:02:08.254 --> 00:02:09.014
Barry shook his head.

35
00:02:09.034 --> 00:02:12.056
"How did you get Gourmet Greta to come and review the diner?

36
00:02:12.417 --> 00:02:13.077
Did you bribe her?"

37
00:02:14.058 --> 00:02:15.359
"What?" Ray growled.

38
00:02:15.379 --> 00:02:18.000
"I'd never do something like that!"

39
00:02:18.961 --> 00:02:20.962
Barry threw his hands up and forced a laugh.

40
00:02:22.323 --> 00:02:23.384
"I was just kidding!

41
00:02:24.585 --> 00:02:27.947
I only meant that restaurant owners are always trying to get Greta to review them.

42
00:02:28.287 --> 00:02:29.168
How did you manage it?"

43
00:02:31.556 --> 00:02:36.259
"She probably heard about how delicious his food is," Ally said loyally.

44
00:02:36.279 --> 00:02:40.121
"Yeah, that makes sense," Barry said.

45
00:02:40.141 --> 00:02:41.421
"I'm sure you're right."

46
00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:46.984
He gushed for a few minutes about Ray's cooking, but Ally couldn't tell if Barry actually meant what

47
00:02:47.024 --> 00:02:47.585
he was saying.

48
00:02:48.525 --> 00:02:51.207
Something about Barry was beginning to strike her as odd.

49
00:02:52.007 --> 00:02:54.308
Still, she'd been on Earth for only a little while.

50
00:02:54.748 --> 00:02:57.510
There was a lot she still didn't understand about human behavior.

51
00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:01.152
Barry ate another bite of his sandwich and then looked at his watch.

52
00:03:01.952 --> 00:03:02.653
"I've got to get home.

53
00:03:02.993 --> 00:03:05.795
My father is expecting me," he added quickly.

54
00:03:05.815 --> 00:03:09.417
"See you tomorrow."

55
00:03:11.458 --> 00:03:13.200
And with that, he raced out of the diner.

56
00:03:14.801 --> 00:03:15.861
Randy scratched his head.

57
00:03:15.881 --> 00:03:17.903
"He's an odd one."

58
00:03:18.823 --> 00:03:19.424
Ally nodded.

59
00:03:20.004 --> 00:03:22.426
"I hope we didn't make a mistake by hiring him."

60
00:03:23.366 --> 00:03:23.987
Ray shrugged.

61
00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:28.149
"You were odd at first too, Ally," he said, laughing.

62
00:03:28.169 --> 00:03:30.591
"I was, wasn't I?"

63
00:03:31.171 --> 00:03:31.792
Ally grinned.

64
00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:34.493
"And look how great I worked out!"

65
00:03:39.556 --> 00:03:41.617
Later Ally returned to her pod in the park.

66
00:03:42.418 --> 00:03:45.680
She took off her meld medallion and reverted to her Astralian form.

67
00:03:50.002 --> 00:03:50.542
She stretched.

68
00:03:50.562 --> 00:03:53.304
"That feels so much better."

69
00:03:54.265 --> 00:03:57.867
As Ally sat down at the control panel, the computer whirled to life.

70
00:03:57.887 --> 00:04:00.028
"Scanning the area.

71
00:04:00.808 --> 00:04:04.371
And detecting no new parts or fuel cells in the immediate vicinity."

72
00:04:05.291 --> 00:04:05.952
Ally sighed.

73
00:04:05.972 --> 00:04:07.893
"Bad news, Alpha.

74
00:04:08.253 --> 00:04:09.274
I couldn't find them.

75
00:04:09.754 --> 00:04:11.395
I'll have to search again tomorrow."

76
00:04:11.415 --> 00:04:14.698
"Searching is unnecessary," the computer said.

77
00:04:14.718 --> 00:04:19.981
"I have computed the exact location of the fuel cells and parts required to repair this pod."

78
00:04:20.862 --> 00:04:22.183
"What?" Ally cried.

79
00:04:22.203 --> 00:04:24.224
"That's fabulous news!

80
00:04:24.885 --> 00:04:25.645
Where are they?"

81
00:04:26.526 --> 00:04:28.127
The computer spat out a printout.

82
00:04:29.047 --> 00:04:29.668
Ally grabbed it.

83
00:04:30.552 --> 00:04:31.833
But her face quickly fell.

84
00:04:31.853 --> 00:04:35.696
"The parts are in the Sandville UFO Museum?"

85
00:04:36.176 --> 00:04:36.796
She groaned.

86
00:04:36.816 --> 00:04:39.298
"That can't be right, Alpha.

87
00:04:39.758 --> 00:04:40.919
I went there this morning.

88
00:04:41.579 --> 00:04:43.921
They don't sell anything we need in the gift shop."

89
00:04:43.941 --> 00:04:49.485
"The items are not in the gift shop," the computer said.

90
00:04:49.505 --> 00:04:52.587
"They are located in the museum's northeast quadrant."

91
00:04:52.607 --> 00:04:56.630
"Huh?" The computer printed out another document.

92
00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:00.092
This one showed a map of the museum.

93
00:05:01.936 --> 00:05:05.058
Ally studied it closely and then let out an even louder groan.

94
00:05:06.118 --> 00:05:09.560
"I know this location—it's Dr.

95
00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:10.661
Lloyd's office!"

96
00:05:13.642 --> 00:05:15.984
She jumped to her feet and started pacing around the pod.

97
00:05:16.444 --> 00:05:17.745
She thought as hard as she could.

98
00:05:19.746 --> 00:05:22.587
But there was only one option: she'd have to go to Dr.

99
00:05:22.607 --> 00:05:23.868
Lloyd's opening on Friday.
